{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1370479-new-shard-brainstorming-the-world-at-war","id":1370479,"title":"[New Shard Brainstorming] the World at War","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-25T18:32:05-08:00","id":1370479,"title":"[New Shard Brainstorming] the World at War","content":"Having an easy night at work that's giving me a lot of time to think (uh oh!), and my mind wandered into thinking of a Modern Shard adaptation based on World War II. I can't be the only one to think of this though. Has anyone else considered it?<br /> <br /> It works pretty well though. Personalities like Roosevelt, Churchill, MacArthur and Montgomery almost are already Solar archetypes. The Soviets would have Alchemicals of course. And I'm loving the mental images I'm having of Abyssals in jackboots and trenchcoats.<br /> <br /> Obviously not in the Real World, so need to figure out how to plot it out in Creation or a similar world. Also, not sure how to fit in a pseudo-Japan. <br /> <br /> Just some early thoughts but thought I'd share. Feel free to share your own","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T07:02:30-08:00","id":1370545,"title":"","content":"I ran an Exalted game that started in the 1920s where the Solars and Lunar Exaltations became known to the world in 1916 and the predominently Dragon-Blooded (and Sidereal) backed establishment was trying to keep a handle on things now that there was a large group of new Exalts who were unaccsutomed to priviledge.<br /> <br /> It was a mix of historical fiction and pulpy elements from early 20th century fiction. For example, Hollow Earth theory was real that's where the Mountain Folk live.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T13:20:04-08:00","id":1370633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1370479-new-shard-brainstorming-the-world-at-war#post1370479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having an easy night at work that's giving me a lot of time to think (uh oh!), and my mind wandered into thinking of a Modern Shard adaptation based on World War II. I can't be the only one to think of this though. Has anyone else considered it?<br /> <br /> It works pretty well though. Personalities like Roosevelt, Churchill, MacArthur and Montgomery almost are already Solar archetypes. <b>The Soviets would have Alchemicals of course.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that association is more than a little overplayed. The industrialized states of the era can all play the collective part of the Octet. They'd probably all want more reliably-produced Champions than gambling on getting other Exalted popping up among their ranks and towing the line (something that Exalted very rarely do without a pre-existing society of their own to get them to fall in line).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T13:55:26-08:00","id":1370641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1370479-new-shard-brainstorming-the-world-at-war?p=1370633#post1370633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that association is more than a little overplayed. The industrialized states of the era can all play the collective part of the Octet. They'd probably all want more reliably-produced Champions than gambling on getting other Exalted popping up among their ranks and towing the line (something that Exalted very rarely do without a pre-existing society of their own to get them to fall in line).</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel that [EXALT TYPE] = [NATIONALITY] in general isn't a good idea. It leads to some very disturbing and racist implications. <br /> The Sun wouldn't consider a German, Japanese, Italian, any Axis man for Exaltation? Not any of the people who designed and built the world's largest warship? Not any of the deadliest fighter pilots? Not some of the most effective demagogues of the time? Not any brave and selfless soldier committing some desperate act of heroism? Because the highest moral authority, the most virtuous being possible, says these people cannot be worthy? <br /> Conversely, only Nazis can be Abyssals? There's no horrible people among the Allies COUGHSTALINCOUGH worthy of that dark power? Not a single desperate figure grasping and straining who'd accept a terrible bargain with death? Not even one? <br /> That's a <i>very</i> delicate line to cross.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T15:45:43-08:00","id":1370671,"title":"","content":"For my game, I loosely defined the new Exalt types in terms of their roles in the Great War.<br /> <br /> Solars were the larger than life heroes of propaganda stories.<br /> Lunars were the more low-key heroes who didn't particularly want to be there.<br /> Abyssals were the people who didn't come back, at least not whole.<br /> Infernals were the people who never went but hurt all the same.<br /> <br /> Alchemicals were different for obvious reasons, the Soviets were the ones who discovered Alchemical Exaltation but they didn't have sole providence over it. Indeed by 1930 the Sidereal PC had made one with the soul of a terminally ill Greek girl and was starting to be pressured into telling the other Sidereals the secret to level the playing field against the Russians but his concern was where the European powers would get the necessary Soulsteel. He had serious concerns of a replay of the Scramble for Africa playing out again in the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T13:21:58-08:00","id":1370830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1370479-new-shard-brainstorming-the-world-at-war?p=1370641#post1370641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel that [EXALT TYPE] = [NATIONALITY] in general isn't a good idea. It leads to some very disturbing and racist implications.<br /> The Sun wouldn't consider a German, Japanese, Italian, any Axis man for Exaltation? Not any of the people who designed and built the world's largest warship? Not any of the deadliest fighter pilots? Not some of the most effective demagogues of the time? Not any brave and selfless soldier committing some desperate act of heroism? Because the highest moral authority, the most virtuous being possible, says these people cannot be worthy?<br /> Conversely, only Nazis can be Abyssals? There's no horrible people among the Allies COUGHSTALINCOUGH worthy of that dark power? Not a single desperate figure grasping and straining who'd accept a terrible bargain with death? Not even one?<br /> That's a <i>very</i> delicate line to cross.</div> </div> </div> </div>Abyssals don't have to be horrible people, even if their power is dark. Their Exaltation process is generally under the tight control of scary necromancers who also happen to be among the dead, though, so that probably leaps into an assumption about some other agency getting into the driver's seat of the process and steering it toward their own ends. It'd probably be another process fought over, of course, like with Alchemical Exaltations; forces marshal to maintain strategic control over Monstrances or whatever stands in for them, and thus the number of potential Abyssals. They'd probably be another force favored over unpredictable Solar and Lunar Exalted. Infernals might as well, leading to a rather dreary setting with a state similar to the world in the WW2 superhero deconstruction comic Uber (apologies for not using the umlaut)<br /> <br /> Also, I would have named Churchill as someone terrible among the Allies. His treatment of India as a colonial overseer was flatly abhorrent, and would have been worse had Stalin not sent grain over for famine relief.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T16:11:40-08:00","id":1370874,"title":"","content":"Personally I didn't have Abyssals linked to Monstrances, because I reasoned anyone with that kind of control over an entire exalt type would be the main antagonist to a setting warping degree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1370479-new-shard-brainstorming-the-world-at-war?p=1370830#post1370830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I would have named Churchill as someone terrible among the Allies. His treatment of India as a colonial overseer was flatly abhorrent, and would have been worse had Stalin not sent grain over for famine relief.</div> </div> </div> </div>Churchill was probably going to be an antagonistic force in Roaring20s because the British Dragon-Blooded PC was in favour of moving India over to dominion status, something which Churchill and the Conservatives strongly opposed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T03:44:36-08:00","id":1370969,"title":"","content":"No one said Solars were always good guys<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not giving up on Abyssals in jackboots though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T03:50:12-08:00","id":1370970,"title":"","content":"Fascism did (and does) love its death-iconography.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}